From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:11:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add a setting to decorate text/plain by wrapping it

Decorating a single-part text/plain message joins the header and footer
to the text, which decodes and re-encodes the body, so a utf-8 body
usually goes out as base64 with every line changed.  Other content types
are decorated by wrapping the message in a multipart/mixed instead.

The new [mailman] decorate_plain_text_in_place setting defaults to 'yes'
to keep current behavior.  With 'no', text/plain is wrapped too and its
body reaches recipients as the sender wrote it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
